from rivers_author import *
U=[]
U.append(unit('穩態水頭基線~Steady hydraulic baseline',
'水錘計算的初始狀態必須同時滿足水量與能量守恆，不能任意指定互不相容的流量及兩端水位。長管摩阻、局部閥損與泵揚程共同決定速度，而高程圖決定每處壓力水頭；相同總壓降並不表示沿線最低壓位置相同。~A transient calculation needs an initial state satisfying both continuity and energy balance. Flow and boundary levels cannot be chosen independently when they are incompatible. Distributed friction, local valve losses and pump head determine velocity, while the elevation profile determines pressure head at each location. Equal total head loss does not imply the same location of minimum pressure.',
'本單元的達西公式假設滿管單相穩定流，所給摩阻係數已另行確定；它不能描述壓力波到達前後的瞬間局部加速度。~The Darcy example assumes steady, single-phase full-pipe flow with a separately established friction factor. It does not describe local acceleration as a pressure wave arrives.',
'假設L=5000 m、D=1 m、v=2 m/s、f=0.020、g=9.81 m/s²，hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=20.39 m，未含局部損失。~Assume L=5000 m, D=1 m, v=2 m/s, f=0.020 and g=9.81 m/s²; hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=20.39 m, excluding local losses.',
'將同步流量、上游水位與下游壓力換算到同一高程基準，逐段對照管徑及粗糙度，另列閥門局部損失。先用未參與校準的穩態時段驗證水頭線，再將可信初值交給瞬變模型。~Convert synchronized flow, upstream level and downstream pressure to one elevation datum, checking diameter and roughness segment by segment and listing valve losses separately. Validate the hydraulic grade using a steady period withheld from calibration before transferring initial conditions to the transient model.',
'若初始水頭線不閉合，數值模型可能在尚未操作閥門前就產生人造波動；這種啟動誤差會被誤判成管線反射或真實水錘。~An inconsistent initial hydraulic grade can create artificial oscillations before any valve action. Such startup errors may then be misidentified as physical reflections or actual water hammer.',
'只要知道平均流量，就不必核對沿線高程與壓力。~Knowing average flow removes the need to check elevation and pressure.',
'建立一張包含流量、基準高程及損失項的能量帳，標示哪些資料為量測、哪些為假設；要求相鄰管段交界的水頭與流量相容後才比較瞬變情境。~Prepare an energy ledger containing flow, datum and losses, marking measured and assumed quantities. Require compatible head and flow at adjacent pipe interfaces before comparing transient scenarios.'))
U.append(unit('流體管壁耦合波速~Fluid and wall wave speed',
'壓力波速度由水的可壓縮性與管壁徑向柔度共同控制，不能直接使用自由水體的聲速。薄壁鋼管的直徑厚度比越大，壁面變形通常越明顯；錨定、泊松效應、襯層及含氣量則會改變有效柔度和頻散，需與管材模型一起選定。~Pressure-wave speed depends jointly on water compressibility and radial pipe-wall compliance, so the sound speed in unconfined water is insufficient. A larger diameter-to-thickness ratio generally increases thin steel-wall deformation. Restraint, Poisson coupling, linings and entrained air change effective compliance and dispersion, requiring a wave-speed model consistent with pipe material and installation.',
'下式為忽略泊松與端部約束修正的簡化彈性薄壁關係，不能直接套用黏彈性塑膠管或有大氣囊的管路。~The expression is a simplified thin elastic-wall relation without Poisson or end-restraint corrections. It does not directly represent viscoelastic plastic pipes or large trapped-air pockets.',
'假設水K=2.2 GPa、ρ=1000 kg/m³、鋼E=200 GPa、D=1 m、t=0.010 m，a=√[K/{ρ(1+KD/Et)}]=1023.5 m/s。~Assume water K=2.2 GPa, ρ=1000 kg/m³, steel E=200 GPa, D=1 m and t=0.010 m; a=√[K/{ρ(1+KD/Et)}]=1023.5 m/s.',
'以管材證明、壁厚檢查及支承配置建立參數範圍，對照經核准的小擾動壓力到時資料估算有效波速。分別檢查溫度與含氣變化，避免只靠調整波速補償錯誤的管長。~Build parameter ranges from material records, thickness inspection and restraint details, then compare effective speed with approved small-disturbance pressure arrival data. Examine temperature and entrained-air changes separately so that speed adjustments do not conceal an incorrect pipe length.',
'把自由水聲速當成全線波速會錯估到時與反射疊加，可能把兩個壓力峰排成錯誤時序；過度調參仍可讓單點曲線看似吻合。~Using free-water sound speed throughout the main distorts arrival times and reflection superposition, potentially ordering pressure peaks incorrectly. Excessive calibration can still make one monitoring trace appear convincing.',
'水錘波速永遠等於水中聲速且與管壁無關。~Water-hammer speed always equals water sound speed regardless of the wall.',
'比較相同直徑下兩種壁厚的計算波速，再列出公式未涵蓋的約束與含氣條件；以多測點到時共同檢驗參數，不用單一峰值選定波速。~Compare two wall thicknesses at the same diameter and list omitted restraint and air conditions. Test the parameters using arrivals at multiple sensors rather than selecting speed from one peak.'))
U.append(unit('快速速度變化與壓升~Rapid velocity change and surge',
'速度突然改變時，液柱動量藉由壓力波與管壁變形重新分配。焦可夫斯基關係把單一波前兩側的速度變化連到壓力變化，但流向、反射、分岔與既有壓力必須分別保留；算出的增量既不是絕對壓力，也不是全系統各處的最大包絡。~A sudden velocity change redistributes liquid momentum through a pressure wave and wall deformation. The Joukowsky relation connects changes across a single wavefront, while flow direction, reflections, branches and initial pressure remain separate. Its calculated increment is neither absolute pressure nor a universal maximum envelope for every point in the system.',
'此算例假設快速變化、單相液體與已知有效波速，尚未處理空化、水柱分離或多波重疊，不能作閥門操作設定。~This example assumes a rapid change, single-phase liquid and known effective speed. Cavitation, column separation and overlapping waves remain outside the calculation and preclude using it as a valve setting.',
'假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=1000 m/s、減速幅度Δv=1.0 m/s，壓升幅度Δp=ρaΔv=1.00 MPa；ΔH=Δp/(ρg)=101.94 m。~Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=1000 m/s and deceleration magnitude Δv=1.0 m/s. Surge magnitude Δp=ρaΔv=1.00 MPa and ΔH=Δp/(ρg)=101.94 m.',
'在壓力紀錄上標示初始值、波前到時與閥位時間軸，同時以流量資料核對速度變化的方向。對每一測點保留儀器頻寬與飽和範圍，確認尖峰未因濾波被削低。~Mark initial pressure, wavefront arrival and valve-position timing on pressure records, checking the velocity-change direction against flow measurements. Retain instrument bandwidth and saturation limits for every sensor and verify that filtering has not suppressed the recorded peaks.',
'將壓力增量誤當總壓力可能漏掉高初始靜壓；反過來把理想正壓升套到所有位置，又會忽視上游或高點可能出現的負壓。~Treating the increment as total pressure overlooks a high initial static pressure. Applying the ideal positive surge everywhere also misses low-pressure behavior at upstream locations or elevated points.',
'焦可夫斯基壓升就是全線的絕對最大壓力。~The Joukowsky increment is the absolute maximum pressure everywhere.',
'用同一初始水頭分別畫出正負速度擾動的第一波，標出增量與總量。再說明哪些邊界反射必須由瞬變求解器補足，保持教學估算與運轉指令分離。~Draw the first waves from positive and negative velocity disturbances using one initial head, distinguishing increments from totals. Identify reflections requiring a transient solver and keep the teaching estimate separate from operating instructions.'))
U.append(unit('往返時間與邊界反射~Round-trip timing and reflections',
'閥門看到的壓力歷程取決於波傳到上游邊界再返回的時間，長度與波速共同決定往返尺度。定水頭水庫與封閉端對壓力波具有不同反射條件，分岔還會依阻抗分配波動；把整條管線視為單一長度可能掩蓋支線的較短共振路徑。~The pressure history at a valve depends on wave travel to the upstream boundary and back. Length and wave speed establish this round-trip scale. A constant-head reservoir and a closed end reflect pressure differently, while branches divide waves according to impedance. Representing the entire network by one length can conceal shorter resonant paths through branches.',
'往返時間只是單一均勻管段的傳播尺度，不是任意管網的完整週期；邊界的動態特性也可能隨閥位與水位改變。~Round-trip time describes propagation along one uniform reach rather than a complete period for any network. Boundary dynamics can also change with valve position and water level.',
'假設均勻管長L=5000 m、波速a=1000 m/s，往返時間Tr=2L/a=10.0 s；關閥時間Tc=3 s時，Tc/Tr=0.30。~Assume uniform length L=5000 m and speed a=1000 m/s. Round-trip time Tr=2L/a=10.0 s; for closure time Tc=3 s, Tc/Tr=0.30.',
'用實際管段與連通圖建立到時表，核對水庫、盲端及支線位置，再比較多支壓力計的首波和回波。若回波順序不符，先查閥門連通狀態，不直接調整阻尼掩蓋拓樸錯誤。~Build an arrival-time table from actual reaches and connectivity, verifying reservoirs, dead ends and branches against first and returning waves at several pressure sensors. If echo ordering disagrees, investigate valve connectivity before adjusting damping to conceal a topology error.',
'錯把開放水庫端設成封閉端會改變壓力反射符號，回波可能由抵消變成疊加；即使首波幅值正確，後續峰值仍會完全失真。~Modeling an open reservoir as a closed boundary changes the pressure-reflection sign and can turn cancellation into reinforcement. Later peaks can therefore be seriously wrong even when the first-wave amplitude matches.',
'管線長度相同就必定具有相同反射歷程。~Equal pipeline lengths necessarily produce identical reflection histories.',
'製作一段水庫至閥門與一段含支線管路的時間距離圖，逐一標明反射邊界。使用到時順序辨認模型結構，再用幅值評估阻抗與損失參數。~Prepare time-distance diagrams for a reservoir-to-valve reach and a branched main, labeling every reflecting boundary. Use arrival order to assess model structure before using amplitudes to assess impedance and losses.'))
U.append(unit('關閉曲線與慢變近似~Closure shape and slow-change approximation',
'關閥總時間不能完整描述水錘，因為有效流通面積與閥桿位置通常不是線性關係。末段的小位移可能造成最大的流量變化，因此相同總時間的兩條關閉曲線可能有不同峰值；慢變估式適合分辨慣性尺度，不能代替真實閥特性與管線反射。~Total closure duration does not fully describe water hammer because effective flow area is usually nonlinear with stem position. Small movement near closure can produce the largest flow change, giving two schedules with equal duration different peaks. A slow-change estimate helps isolate inertia but cannot replace actual valve characteristics and reflected waves.',
'下式只作簡單水庫至閥門管線、假設近似均勻減速且關閉較慢的量級比較；不保證為實際峰值上限，也不是推薦關閉時間。~The expression is a scale comparison for a simple reservoir-to-valve main with approximately uniform deceleration and slow closure. It is not a guaranteed peak bound or a recommended closure time.',
'假設L=5000 m、v0=1 m/s、Tc=30 s、g=9.81 m/s²，慢變比較ΔH≈2Lv0/(gTc)=33.98 m；此例Tr=10 s。~Assume L=5000 m, v0=1 m/s, Tc=30 s and g=9.81 m/s². A slow-change comparison gives ΔH≈2Lv0/(gTc)=33.98 m, with Tr=10 s in this example.',
'取得製造商閥位與流量係數關係，將實測行程時間轉成有效開度歷程，分別重算前段及末段變化。以核准的離線情境比較全線壓力包絡，檢查供水需求及機械行程限制。~Obtain the manufacturer’s position-to-flow-coefficient relationship and convert measured travel timing into effective opening history, examining early and final portions separately. Compare pressure envelopes in approved offline scenarios while checking supply requirements and mechanical travel constraints.',
'只將整體關閉時間拉長，卻保留末段突關，仍可能產生強烈壓升；模型若把閥位直接當流量比例，會錯誤預測緩閉措施已奏效。~Increasing overall duration while retaining abrupt final closure can still create a strong surge. A model that equates valve position with flow fraction may incorrectly predict that a slow-closing measure is effective.',
'關閉時間增加一倍就一定讓全線峰值減半。~Doubling closure time always halves the peak everywhere in the main.',
'比較兩條總時間相同但末段速度不同的假設閥位曲線，說明需加入哪一份流量係數資料才能計算。報告只討論敏感度，不把結果寫成現場閥門設定。~Compare hypothetical schedules with equal duration but different final travel rates, identifying the flow-coefficient data needed for calculation. Report sensitivity without converting the outcome into field valve settings.'))
U.append(unit('停泵慣性與能量尺度~Pump rundown inertia and energy scale',
'停電後泵組不會瞬間停止，轉子與液柱慣性共同決定轉速、流量及揚程的變化。泵可能經過零流量甚至逆流區，正常運轉的單一揚程曲線不足以表示全過程；旋轉動能只能提供初步能量尺度，不能以固定功率除法取代轉速相依的動力方程。~After power loss a pump does not stop instantaneously. Rotor and liquid-column inertia jointly determine speed, discharge and head. The machine can pass through zero flow and possibly reverse flow, beyond a single normal operating curve. Rotational energy supplies a preliminary scale, but division by fixed hydraulic power cannot replace the speed-dependent dynamic equation.',
'本例把全部初始轉動能假想轉成固定水力功率，忽略效率、摩擦及揚程變化，只得到比較時間而非實際滑行停機時間。~This example hypothetically converts all initial rotational energy into fixed hydraulic power, omitting efficiency, friction and changing head. Its time is a comparison scale, not actual coastdown duration.',
'假設I=100 kg·m²、ω=100 rad/s，E=Iω²/2=500 kJ；若比較功率P=100 kW，E/P=5.0 s，非停泵預測。~Assume I=100 kg·m² and ω=100 rad/s: E=Iω²/2=500 kJ. For comparison power P=100 kW, E/P=5.0 s, not a rundown prediction.',
'核對馬達、聯軸器與泵的等效轉動慣量，取得可用的四象限性能資料，並同步檢視歷史停泵的轉速、電力與壓力紀錄。量測缺乏逆流資料時，應保留模型區間而非外推正常曲線。~Check equivalent inertia for the motor, coupling and pump, obtain available four-quadrant performance data, and align historical rundown speed, electrical power and pressure records. Where reverse-flow observations are absent, retain model ranges rather than extrapolating the normal operating curve.',
'把泵當作停電即零流量的邊界會製造不實急停，反之忽略止回閥關閉又會漏掉逆流截斷衝擊；兩種錯誤可能在單點壓力上互相抵消。~A zero-flow boundary immediately after power loss creates an artificial stop, while omitting check-valve closure misses reverse-flow interruption. These two errors can misleadingly cancel at one pressure monitoring point.',
'初始轉動能除以額定功率就是精確停泵時間。~Initial rotational energy divided by rated power gives exact rundown time.',
'列出停泵模型需要的慣量、性能圖與止回閥資料，指出能量估式缺少的動態耦合。以假設較大慣量比較能量尺度，另行說明為何峰值不必按比例下降。~List inertia, machine characteristics and check-valve data required for rundown modeling, identifying dynamic couplings omitted by the energy estimate. Compare a larger assumed inertia and explain why pressure peaks need not fall proportionally.'))
U.append(unit('低壓與水柱分離~Low pressure and column separation',
'高點或停泵後的低壓波可能使局部絕對壓力接近蒸氣壓，液體連續柱的單相假設因此失效。空穴形成與再閉合會改變波速、流量連續性及二次壓峰，不能讓數值解無限制下降到負絕對壓；溶解氣體析出又與純蒸氣空穴具有不同時間尺度。~At elevated points or after pump shutdown, a low-pressure wave can bring absolute pressure near vapor pressure and invalidate a continuous single-phase column. Cavity formation and collapse alter wave speed, continuity and secondary pressure peaks. A numerical solution must not extend without limit into negative absolute pressure, while dissolved-gas release has different time scales from pure vapor cavities.',
'比較必須使用同一溫度下的絕對壓力與蒸氣壓；正的差值只代表此瞬間尚有壓力裕度，不證明所有位置都不空化。~Compare absolute pressure and vapor pressure at the same temperature. A positive difference indicates a margin at that instant only, not absence of cavitation everywhere.',
'假設局部絕對壓力pabs=30 kPa、該溫度蒸氣壓pv=2.3 kPa，裕度pabs−pv=27.7 kPa；兩者都不是表壓。~Assume local absolute pressure pabs=30 kPa and vapor pressure pv=2.3 kPa at the stated temperature. The margin pabs−pv=27.7 kPa; neither value is gauge pressure.',
'將高程、氣壓、液溫及壓力計零點一併整理，確認低壓量測範圍足以涵蓋預測值。比較單相與適當空穴模型的最低壓和再閉合峰值，並檢查時間步長對空穴體積的影響。~Assemble elevation, atmospheric pressure, liquid temperature and sensor-zero information, confirming that the instrument range covers predicted lows. Compare minimum pressure and collapse peaks between single-phase and suitable cavity models, and examine time-step sensitivity of cavity volume.',
'以表壓直接與蒸氣壓相比會錯置空化判斷，截掉所有負表壓也會消除真實低壓歷程；錯誤的空穴閉合模型可能低估隨後更高的壓峰。~Comparing gauge pressure directly with vapor pressure misclassifies cavitation, while clipping all negative gauge pressure erases real low-pressure behavior. An incorrect cavity-collapse model can underestimate the larger peak that follows.',
'只要表壓小於零，就表示管內已形成蒸氣空穴。~Any negative gauge pressure means a vapor cavity has formed.',
'以同一組氣壓與蒸氣壓資料把三個表壓讀值換成絕對壓，標出哪些需要兩相模型。再討論感測器低壓限幅會如何影響空穴診斷。~Convert three gauge readings to absolute pressure using one atmospheric and vapor-pressure dataset, identifying cases needing a two-phase model. Discuss how low-pressure sensor clipping changes cavity diagnosis.'))
U.append(unit('氣室壓縮與調壓容量~Air-vessel compression and storage',
'氣室藉由可壓縮氣體吸收或供應水量，氣體壓力與體積沿熱力路徑變化。快速過程可能較接近絕熱，慢過程可能交換更多熱量，實際指數須依設備與時間尺度選擇；接管損失、預充狀態與水位行程也限制可用調壓量，不能只看容器總容積。~An air vessel absorbs or supplies water through compression of its gas volume. Pressure and volume evolve along a thermodynamic path: rapid events may approach adiabatic behavior, while slow events permit more heat transfer. The exponent depends on equipment and time scale, and connector losses, precharge condition and water travel constrain usable storage beyond the vessel’s gross volume.',
'多方關係必須使用絕對壓力，且本例假設氣體質量固定；未含氣體溶解、熱交換細節及接管水力損失，不構成容器選型。~The polytropic relation uses absolute pressure and assumes constant gas mass here. It omits gas dissolution, detailed heat transfer and connecting-pipe losses and is not a vessel selection.',
'假設p1=300 kPa絕對壓、V1=2.0 m³、V2=1.8 m³、n=1.2，p2=p1(V1/V2)^n=340.4 kPa絕對壓。~Assume p1=300 kPa absolute, V1=2.0 m³, V2=1.8 m³ and n=1.2. Then p2=p1(V1/V2)^n=340.4 kPa absolute.',
'核對氣室壓力、液位與溫度是否同步，查驗氣體有效容積和接管阻力的資料來源。使用不同多方指數及預充偏差重算完整壓力包絡，檢查是否觸及液位行程與設備限制。~Check synchronization of vessel pressure, water level and temperature, verifying the basis for effective gas volume and connector resistance. Recalculate full pressure envelopes for alternative polytropic exponents and precharge deviations, examining liquid travel and equipment limits.',
'把表壓放入多方關係會算錯氣體剛度，未記錄氣體流失則可能高估可用緩衝；容器外形尺寸不變，實際有效氣量仍會逐步減少。~Using gauge pressure in the polytropic relation miscalculates gas stiffness, and unrecorded gas loss can overstate buffering capacity. The vessel’s external dimensions may stay unchanged while its effective gas volume progressively decreases.',
'調壓氣室的總容積等於任何時刻可用的氣體容積。~Total vessel volume equals usable gas volume at every instant.',
'用相同體積變化比較等溫與較快壓縮的壓力結果，明列絕對壓力基準。畫出氣體與水各占的容積，說明維護量測如何更新模型初始狀態。~Compare isothermal and faster-compression pressures for one volume change, stating the absolute-pressure basis. Draw separate gas and water volumes and explain how maintenance measurements update the model’s initial condition.'))
U.append(unit('特徵線網格與數值耗散~Characteristic grids and numerical damping',
'特徵線方法沿壓力波傳播方向連結水頭與流量，空間和時間步長需與波速相容。為了容納不同管長而插值可能引入數值耗散，造成計算峰值變小且看似穩定；這種人工平滑不能當作物理摩阻的證據，應與實際阻尼和量測頻寬分開評估。~The method of characteristics links head and discharge along wave-propagation directions, requiring compatible spatial and temporal increments. Interpolation used to accommodate different pipe lengths can introduce numerical damping, reducing peaks and making results appear stable. Such artificial smoothing is not evidence of physical friction and must be assessed separately from real damping and measurement bandwidth.',
'本例僅核對單一均勻管段的Courant數；C=1不保證所有非線性邊界或空穴模型都準確，仍需網格收斂與質量守恆檢查。~The example checks the Courant number for one uniform reach only. C=1 does not guarantee accuracy for nonlinear boundaries or cavity models, so convergence and mass balance remain necessary.',
'假設a=1000 m/s、Δt=0.020 s、Δx=20 m，C=aΔt/Δx=1.0；若Δt減半且Δx不變，C=0.50。~Assume a=1000 m/s, Δt=0.020 s and Δx=20 m. C=aΔt/Δx=1.0; halving Δt at fixed Δx gives C=0.50.',
'至少比較兩組相容的空間時間網格，保留最大最小壓力、首波到時及總水量誤差。若細化後峰值持續變化，先檢查插值與邊界實作，再決定是否需要更細模型。~Compare at least two compatible space-time grids, retaining maximum and minimum pressure, first-wave arrival and total water-volume error. If peaks continue changing under refinement, inspect interpolation and boundary implementation before deciding whether further resolution is needed.',
'粗網格的人工耗散可能掩蓋短時壓峰，讓保護設備看似足夠；只看求解器沒有發散，不能證明尖峰或水柱分離已被解析。~Artificial damping on a coarse grid can hide short pressure peaks and make protective equipment appear sufficient. The absence of solver divergence does not prove that peaks or column separation have been resolved.',
'計算曲線越平滑就表示模型越準確而且越安全。~A smoother calculated trace necessarily means a more accurate and safer model.',
'保存同一事件在兩組網格上的壓力包絡及質量帳，以數值差而非圖形平滑度評估收斂。記錄所用插值、波速調整與邊界演算法，讓他人能重算。~Preserve pressure envelopes and mass ledgers for one event on two grids, judging convergence by numerical differences rather than visual smoothness. Record interpolation, wave-speed adjustment and boundary algorithms so another analyst can reproduce the calculation.'))
U.append(unit('循環壓力與管殼疲勞~Cyclic pressure and shell fatigue',
'單次極大壓力與長期重複壓力範圍控制不同的損傷問題。薄壁圓管可把壓力範圍換成名目環向應力範圍，但焊趾、腐蝕坑及支座附近會產生局部集中；疲勞評估還需循環次數、平均應力及細節分類，不能把低於降伏當作無限壽命。~A single extreme pressure and repeated pressure ranges govern different damage mechanisms. A thin circular shell converts pressure range into nominal hoop-stress range, but weld toes, corrosion pits and supports introduce local concentrations. Fatigue assessment also needs cycle counts, mean stress and detail classification; stress below yield does not establish infinite service life.',
'本式假設薄壁均勻圓管與名目膜應力，沒有給定疲勞曲線或應力集中係數，因此只算應力範圍，不預測壽命。~The expression assumes a uniform thin circular shell and nominal membrane stress. No fatigue curve or concentration factor is specified, so it calculates stress range without predicting life.',
'假設壓力範圍Δp=0.40 MPa、D=1.0 m、t=0.010 m，名目環應力範圍Δσ=ΔpD/(2t)=20.0 MPa。~Assume pressure range Δp=0.40 MPa, D=1.0 m and t=0.010 m. Nominal hoop-stress range Δσ=ΔpD/(2t)=20.0 MPa.',
'將足夠取樣頻率的壓力歷程與泵閥事件紀錄對時，再依核定方法作循環計數。結合壁厚、焊接細節及局部缺陷檢查，確認名目應力能否代表疲勞關鍵位置。~Synchronize adequately sampled pressure histories with pump and valve event logs, then count cycles using an approved method. Combine wall thickness, weld detail and local defect inspection to determine whether nominal stress represents the fatigue-critical location.',
'用平均厚度或平均壓力取代局部最薄處及循環範圍，可能嚴重低估焊接細節損傷；漏掉頻繁小事件也會把長期累積效應誤認為偶發破壞。~Replacing minimum local thickness and cycle range with average thickness or pressure can greatly understate welded-detail damage. Missing frequent smaller events also makes cumulative deterioration appear to be an isolated failure.',
'每一次應力都低於降伏強度就完全沒有疲勞問題。~Every stress cycle below yield means fatigue is impossible.',
'以同一壓力範圍比較原始與減薄管壁的名目應力，再列出仍缺少的疲勞資料。將操作事件頻率與檢查位置連結，避免只按單一最大壓力安排維護。~Compare nominal stress for original and thinned walls at one pressure range, then list missing fatigue information. Link event frequency to inspection locations instead of planning maintenance around a single maximum pressure.'))

write('b261','波傳播、邊界反射與輸水瞬變驗證~Wave propagation, boundary reflections and water-main transient verification',
'本課從穩態水頭線開始，依序分析彈性波速、速度突變、邊界反射、關閉曲線及停泵慣性，再把低壓空穴、氣室熱力、數值網格與疲勞接回完整輸水系統。每個算例都分清初步量級與完整瞬變模型，並要求壓力、流量、閥位及時間基準互相驗證。~Starting with the steady hydraulic grade, this course examines elastic wave speed, velocity changes, reflections, closure shape and pump inertia, then connects cavities, air-vessel thermodynamics, numerical grids and fatigue to the complete water-main system. Each example distinguishes a scale estimate from a complete transient model and checks pressure, flow, valve position and timing against one another.',U,
'原創整合算例假設水密度1000 kg/m³、波速1000 m/s與快速減速1.0 m/s，第一波壓升為1.00 MPa。僅將波速增加10%至1100 m/s，其餘條件固定，壓升變成1.10 MPa，同時5000 m管段的往返時間由10.0 s降為9.09 s。這顯示參數改變同時影響幅值與時序，不能只用較大波速替所有不確定度保守包絡。再以三個監測點核對到時、初始壓力與峰值，另列反射、空穴與閥門曲線尚待求解的項目。這些數字不代表任何列名工程的實測或操作門檻。~An original integrated example assumes water density 1000 kg/m³, speed 1000 m/s and rapid deceleration 1.0 m/s, giving a first-wave pressure rise of 1.00 MPa. Increasing only wave speed by 10% to 1100 m/s raises the increment to 1.10 MPa and shortens the round trip in a 5000 m reach from 10.0 to 9.09 s. A parameter change therefore affects amplitude and timing together; a higher speed is not automatically a conservative envelope for all uncertainties. Check arrivals, initial pressure and peaks at three monitoring points, while separately listing reflections, cavities and valve characteristics requiring further solution. These numbers are not measurements or operating thresholds from any named project.',
['usbr-penstocks','epa-epanet','nyc-delaware','sfpuc-moccasin'],PIPE_MARKS,PIPE_PLACE,
[['初始水頭','Initial head'],['波傳管段','Wave-carrying reach'],['閥泵邊界','Valve and pump boundaries'],['調壓設備','Surge protection'],['量測驗證','Measured validation']],PIPE_HISTORY,PIPE_TIMELINE,PIPE_CODES,['b262','b265'])
